From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: steamac <steamac@local>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 19:40:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] kk: one compute trigger write per encoder for timestamps

A timestamp written in a compute encoder needs compute work in that encoder,
so each one recorded a dispatch that rewrote the query's sentinel, between
two barriers. Each barrier takes about 5 KiB of Metal command allocator
memory: vkd3d-proton's 8192 timestamps in one command buffer took 82 MiB of
allocator memory, which the allocator keeps after a reset.

Vulkan requires a reset before a timestamp write, and the reset stores the
sentinel already. Only the first timestamp of an encoder, with no resolve
pending, now records the dispatch.

Generated-by: LLM
---
 src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_query_pool.c | 8 +++++---
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_query_pool.c b/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_query_pool.c
index 3d27579..0b52843 100644
--- a/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_query_pool.c
+++ b/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_query_pool.c
@@ -535,9 +535,11 @@ kk_CmdWriteTimestamp2(VkCommandBuffer commandBuffer,
           * compute work in the encoder to trigger it.  Rewrite the low half of
           * the sentinel the report already holds, which leaves the query
           * unavailable until the resolve lands. */
-         libkk_write_u32(cmd, kk_grid_1d(1), false,
-                         kk_query_report_addr(dev, pool, query),
-                         (uint32_t)LIBKK_QUERY_UNAVAILABLE);
+         if (util_dynarray_num_elements(&cmd->ts_resolves,
+                                        struct kk_ts_resolve) == 0)
+            libkk_write_u32(cmd, kk_grid_1d(1), false,
+                            kk_query_report_addr(dev, pool, query),
+                            (uint32_t)LIBKK_QUERY_UNAVAILABLE);
 
          mtl_compute_write_timestamp(cmd->metal.compute, heap, heap_index);
       }
